<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Errana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · Also known as Errapragada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Errana, or Errapragada, was a 14th-century Telugu poet who completed the Telugu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nannaya">Nannaya</a> and continued by Tikkana. He finished the Aranya Parva, left incomplete by Nannaya, and with the other two is honoured as one of the Kavitrayam, the three poets of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-mahabharatam">Andhra Mahabharatam</a>. He wrote under the patronage of the Reddi kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/errana.jpg" alt="Errana" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pakideadithya · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Errapragada_painting_.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
